          "title": "You'll want to know: परिचारिका",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "परिचारिका — paricārikā — \"a nurse\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "paricārikā is built on pari, \"around\", and the root √car, \"to move, attend upon\" (MW): one who moves around a person to look after them. MW glosses it \"a female attendant\"; the sense \"nurse\" is modern."
            }
          ]
        },
