          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "abhiyantā is a modern coinage, not in MW, built on abhi- and the root √yam, \"to hold, control\", with the agent ending -tṛ. √yam is also the root of yantra, \"device, machine\" (CDIAL 10412), so the engineer is the one who controls the machines."
            }
          ]
        },
